    <briefdescription>
<para>Entry point for the 42sh unit test suite. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>pulgamecanica (arosado-)</para>
</simplesect>
Run with: <computeroutput>make test</computeroutput></para>
<sect1 id="test__runner_8c_1autotoc_md7_1s1"><sect2 id="test__runner_8c_1autotoc_md7">
<title>How to Graduate a Test</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>1. Implement the module under <computeroutput>srcs/MODULE/</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>2. Add <computeroutput>-DTEST_MODULE_ENABLED</computeroutput> to <computeroutput>TEST_FLAGS</computeroutput> in the root Makefile.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>3. Verify all MU_ASSERT lines pass with <computeroutput>make test</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>4. When permanently green:<linebreak/>
 Delete <computeroutput>#ifdef</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>#else</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>#endif</computeroutput> in <computeroutput>tests/test_module.c</computeroutput>.<linebreak/>
 Delete <computeroutput>#ifdef</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>#endif</computeroutput> around MU_RUN() below.<linebreak/>
 Remove <computeroutput>-DTEST_MODULE_ENABLED</computeroutput> from the root Makefile.<linebreak/>
 The test then compiles and runs unconditionally forever. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
